Z||000001||Shiner||10-17-1999||12:09 AM||||The fastback has classic lines.  It will ALWAYS look good, unlike something like the new Celica GT.  Once the rice-boy fad has passed (I am waiting), everyone will hate that car.  My first car was my '84 SC auto.  It was a very good first car, if a little problematic.  One good thing about a fiero for a first car is that you can't carry around a google of friends to distract you.  And if, god forbid, you should get into some horrible crash, you are not going to take out 5 of your best friends with you, like so many teenagers do today.  The SC also helped to keep me out of trouble.  Now I have the '87 GT.  For some reason, I can't keep my foot off the gas  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  That car just beckons to me, "Give me some gas, come on, it's fun" So I comply, and when I look down, I am doubling the speed limit in town.  Not good.  This car is going to get me into alot of trouble.  Since I have a junior lisence (turning 18 soon!), one ticket for 26mph over, I get it revoked.  Or two infractions of and kind, and it gets taken away for 3 months!  This is going to be hard.... but I only have to be good for 3 months.<P>Whatever you do, be safe!  ||||reg||7
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||10-17-1999||12:58 AM||||Shiner...make that be good at all times, no matter what type of license you have.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||10-17-1999||03:18 AM||||GWMORGAN,<BR> But what would be the point of having a GT if I can't occasionally smoke the rear tires, or run it up through the gears?  If I wasn't going to go fast, I would have just kept my '84 SC auto!||||reg||12
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||10-17-1999||03:57 AM||||I partly agree with both of you: <I>"Be good <B>some</B> of the time, but be safe <B>all</B> of the time."</I>||||reg||6
Z||000005||RFMike||10-17-1999||01:39 PM||||And if your going to be bad, be bad where your won't endanger others.<BR>Yesterday was one of those bright blue fall days up here in Wisconsin.  Absolutely gorgeous.  I was out and about, drove over to St. Paul, and saw 4 (count 'em) GT's and 3 notchbacks in the course of the afternoon.  I think a lot of these guys were enjoying the nice weather before putting the car away.<BR>Flashed the thumbs up, got a couple in return.  Good stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000007||GWMORGAN||10-17-1999||03:41 PM||||Shiner,<BR>I understand what you're saying.Just wanted you to be careful,that's all. Go ahead and enjoy your fiero to the fullest.||||reg||1
